{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"256","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Liars and Serge"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" people, sitting in a line at the table. For each person we know that he always tells either the truth or lies."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Little Serge asked them: how many of you always tell the truth? Each of the people at the table knows everything (who is an honest person and who is a liar) about all the people at the table. The honest people are going to say the correct answer, the liars are going to say any integer from 1 to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", which is not the correct answer. Every liar chooses his answer, regardless of the other liars, so two distinct liars may give distinct answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Serge does not know any information about the people besides their answers to his question. He took a piece of paper and wrote "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the answer of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th person in the row. Given this sequence, Serge determined that exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" people sitting at the table "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"apparently lie"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Serge wonders, how many variants of people's answers (sequences of answers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" of length "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":") there are where one can say that exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" people sitting at the table apparently lie. As there can be rather many described variants of answers, count the remainder of dividing the number of the variants by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"777777777"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ k ≤ n ≤ 28)"},{"kind":"text","text":". It is guaranteed that "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" — is the power of number 2."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single integer — the answer to the problem modulo "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"777777777"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"256D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/256/problem/D"}